KZ3 patch 2188 (RSX pass 166, command-thread overhaul O0: probes; diagnostics only, guest-invisible, every output behind a switch, default OFF):
1. RSX_PERF_SPLIT=1: [perf-split] (+ [perf-split-d], [perf-split-o]) per [perf-walk] window, the line format is shared with the Killzone 2 port. Exclusive
   buckets from a stack in new libs/video/rsx_o0.h: the walker's clock is charged to the innermost open bucket, so the buckets add
   up to the pass time by construction; decode_f (CG word loop) and decode_d (rsx_dispatch_method minus its sinks) are separate in
   [perf-split-d] and summed in decode=. Needs RSX_PERF's reporter (implied); without RSX_PERF_PROF=A,B it measures the whole run.
   gpu= is the RSX_PERF_GPU=1 fence poller's busy time (-1 when it is off).
2. RSX_O0=1: [o0-state] [o0-4b] [o0-ref] [o0-seg] [o0-tex] [o0-tex-src] [o0-wbov] once per second (tex-src every 5th).
Off = one int test per hook (g_rsx_split_act / g_rsx_o0.on) and the sink wrappers are not installed.
